license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-28"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark for causal, constrained, dynamical decision-making. It scores predictions and
  decisions on the axis each deserves, so a gradient-boosted tree can win one-step prediction
  while a causal, constrained controller wins the closed loop. Eleven tracks cover one-step and
  rollout prediction, counterfactual effect recovery under confounding, oracle-regret control,
  lagged-structure discovery, impulse-response (dynamic) effects, offline incentive allocation
  when SUTVA fails through a shared equilibrium, control under partial identification where no
  adjustment set exists, and causal identification of the control channel on two live external
  plants: a BOPTEST building emulator logged by a weather-compensated controller, and
  Gymnasium's Pendulum-v1, whose channel is known exactly. Results are committed as tables with
  multi-seed bootstrap confidence intervals.
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - causal inference
  - optimal control
  - model predictive control
  - offline reinforcement learning
  - interference
  - partial identification
  - jax
